#: ../../book/open-models.rst:1
msgid ""
"Chapter 4: How open-source AI was released before export controls (4-step "
"midnight git push) versus how it navigates 4 checkpoints under "
"Announcement 48 and US EAR rules."
msgstr ""
"第4章：开源人工智能在出口管制前如何发布（四步“午夜 git push”无国界直达），以及如今如何在第48号公告与美国 EAR "
"规则下穿过四道合规关闸。"

#: ../../book/open-models.rst:5
msgid "04. Open-Source AI Before and After the Walls"
msgstr "04. 高墙前后的开源人工智能"

#: ../../book/open-models.rst:8
msgid "The Golden Midnight Upload: How Open AI Used to Reach Humanity"
msgstr "黄金时代的“午夜上传”：开源 AI 曾如何直抵全人类"

#: ../../book/open-models.rst:11
msgid ""
"To feel what is at stake for human progress, rewind to how an open-source "
"AI breakthrough entered the world before export controls caught up with "
"neural networks."
msgstr ""
"要想真切体会今天这场变革究竟牵动着人类进步的哪根神经，不妨把时钟倒拨回去，看看在出口管制的目光追上神经网络之前，一项开源人工智能突破是怎样来到这个世界上的。"

#: ../../book/open-models.rst:16
msgid ""
"Before and after the border gates: on the left, open-source breakthroughs "
"radiated straight from laboratory benches across the globe; on the right, "
"new releases pass through classification arches and statutory scales "
"before reaching the open commons."
msgstr ""
"边境设闸前后的鲜明对照：左侧，开源突破曾从实验室工作台无拘无束地辐射全球；右侧，新发布的模型须依次穿过分级拱门与法定天平，方能汇入开放知识公地。"

#: ../../book/open-models.rst:18
msgid ""
"Suppose twenty engineers in Hangzhou, Paris, or San Francisco finished "
"training a remarkable reasoning model on a Tuesday night. Their entire "
"global release pipeline had **four steps**:"
msgstr ""
"设想在杭州、巴黎或旧金山的某个周二深夜，二十名年轻工程师刚刚完成了一款推理大模型的最后一次训练收敛。他们面向全世界发布成果的完整流程，总共只有 "
"**短短四步** ："

#: ../../book/open-models.rst:20
msgid ""
"**Finish internal benchmarks and safety checks** on the trained weights "
"and inference code."
msgstr "**完成内部基准评测与安全对齐检查** ，确认训练好的模型权重与推理代码运行稳健。"

#: ../../book/open-models.rst:21
msgid ""
"**Attach a permissive copyright license**, a short text file like the "
"**MIT License** (used by DeepSeek for its flagship DeepSeek-R1 code and "
"weights) or **Apache License 2.0** (used by Alibaba's Qwen team for its "
"Qwen3 family) ``[R1]`` ``[QWEN]``."
msgstr ""
"**附上一份宽松的开源版权许可证**，一段简短的纯文本文件，例如 **MIT 许可证** （DeepSeek 旗舰模型 DeepSeek-R1 "
"的代码与权重均采用此协议）或 **Apache License 2.0** （阿里巴巴通义千问团队 Qwen3 全系列采用此协议） "
"``[R1]`` ``[QWEN]`` 。"

#: ../../book/open-models.rst:22
msgid ""
"**Run** ``git push`` **and upload the weight files** to global public "
"hubs like Hugging Face, GitHub, and ModelScope alongside a technical "
"paper."
msgstr ""
"**敲下** ``git push`` **并上传权重文件** ，连同一篇详尽的技术报告同步发布到 Hugging Face、GitHub "
"与魔搭社区（ModelScope）等全球公共托管平台。"

#: ../../book/open-models.rst:23
msgid "**Go to sleep** while the rest of humanity woke up and built."
msgstr "**关灯安睡**，地球另一端醒来的人们，已在晨光中接过火炬开始创造。"

#: ../../book/open-models.rst:25
msgid ""
"No customs lawyer was retained. No provincial bureau stamped an export "
"sheet. By Wednesday afternoon, an agronomist in Brazil was fine-tuning "
"that model to spot cassava blight on cheap phones; a student in Seoul was "
"quantizing it to run on a laptop GPU; a hospital team in Berlin was "
"summarizing discharge notes behind its own air-gapped server without "
"sending a single patient's name to a foreign cloud."
msgstr ""
"其间无需聘请海关合规律师，也无需等待省级厅局在审批单上落印盖章。到了周三下午，巴西的农学家已经在用它微调出一款能在百元旧手机上识别木薯枯萎病的助手；首尔的大学生已将它量化压缩进笔记本显卡；柏林的医院信息团队更已在物理断网的院内服务器上用它整理出院病历摘要，连一个患者的姓名都无需发往任何境外商业云端。"

#: ../../book/open-models.rst:29
msgid ""
"**Open weights vs. Open Source AI:** Releasing downloadable weights under "
"MIT or Apache 2.0 is precisely called *open weights*, whereas the Open "
"Source Initiative's **Open Source AI Definition 1.0** asks for code, "
"parameters, and enough training-data detail to substantially recreate the "
"system ``[OSI]``. Export regulators, however, care far less about "
"terminology than about what concrete files and hardware capabilities "
"cross a border."
msgstr ""
"**“开放权重”与严格意义上的“开源人工智能”：** 以 MIT 或 Apache 2.0 协议公开可下载的模型参数，在技术上准确称为 "
"*开放权重（Open Weights）* ；而国际开源促进会（OSI）发布的 **《开源人工智能定义 1.0》** "
"则要求同时公开代码、模型参数以及足以实质复现该系统的训练数据说明 ``[OSI]`` "
"。不过，在出口管制监管者眼中，学术命名之争并不重要，他们真正关心的是究竟有哪些具体文件与硬件能力跨越了国境。"

#: ../../book/open-models.rst:31
msgid "How Export Controls Transform the Open-Source Release Pipeline"
msgstr "出口管制如何重塑开源发布全流程"

#: ../../book/open-models.rst:34
msgid ""
"Now trace that exact same Tuesday-night release under **China's "
"Announcement 48** and parallel **US EAR rules**. The journey from "
"laboratory compute cluster to global developer is no longer an unguarded "
"midnight bridge; it passes through four structured checkpoints ``[CN48]`` "
"``[CN-A1]`` ``[CNQA]`` ``[EAR734]``:"
msgstr ""
"现在，让我们把同一个周二深夜的模型发布放进 **中国第48号公告** 与 **美国 EAR 规则** "
"的双重聚光灯下重新走一遍。从实验室算力集群通往全球开发者的道路，已不再是一座无人值守的午夜石桥，而必须依次穿过四道结构分明的合规关闸 "
"``[CN48]`` ``[CN-A1]`` ``[CNQA]`` ``[EAR734]`` ："

